workedExamples.question_text:
An interior angle $I$ and its adjacent exterior angle $E$ are shown at a vertex of a regular polygon.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (-2,0)--(0,0)--(1.6,0);
\draw[black] (0,0)--(-1,1.732);
\draw[black] (0.55,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=120,radius=0.55];
\draw[black] (-0.8,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=120,radius=0.8];
\path (0.48,0.83) node {$E$};
\path (-1.05,0.58) node {$I$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. If $E=36^{\circ}$, find $I$.
b. For another regular polygon, $I=156^{\circ}$. Find $E$.
The diagram is not drawn to scale.

